<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.Lluciocc.Groovia</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>

  <name>Groovia</name>
  <summary>Your local music, beautifully organized.</summary>

  <description>
    <p>Groovia is a local music player for GNOME that makes a personal collection feel like a record shelf. It scans folders in the background, groups tracks into albums, reads embedded metadata and artwork, and keeps the library in a local database.</p>
    <p>The player combines GStreamer playback with an animated vinyl deck, a responsive queue, configurable crossfade, gapless playback, ReplayGain normalization, notifications, and MPRIS controls where supported. Album artwork can shape the interface's color palette, while animations and other visual options can be adjusted in Preferences.</p>
    <p>Organize music with playlists and favorites, search and sort tracks, create custom playlist covers, and play common local formats including MP3, FLAC, Ogg Vorbis, Opus, WAV, AAC, and M4A.</p>
    <p>Optional Spotify imports use spotDL to find matching audio and preserve playlist metadata and artwork. Groovia does not stream or download audio directly from Spotify. Synchronized and plain lyrics can be imported, downloaded when supported, edited locally, and displayed line by line or word by word.</p>
    <p>Auto DJ is an opt-in feature that analyzes tracks in the background and plans queue-safe transitions using phrase, silence, beat, tempo, and bass information when available. It keeps the queue intact and falls back gracefully when advanced audio processing is unavailable.</p>
  </description>

  <developer id="tld.vendor">
    <name>Lluciocc</name>
  </developer>

